Octave Blocks 0.3.0 (development)

Adds compiled acceleration, flat adaptive C export, Transport Delay,
Limited Integrator, programmatic modeling and recorded Simulink evidence.
The combined distribution is GPL-3.0-or-later to include adapted Octave
solver components; original MIT notices remain in LICENSES/MIT.txt.

Uses GNU Octave package conventions: inst/ for installed functions,
inst/private/ for shared implementation, doc/ for documentation, and
DESCRIPTION, COPYING and INDEX for package installation and discovery.
Examples are installed separately from the public API in inst/examples/.
Tests and benchmarks remain in tests/ and are not added by pkg load.

New Simulink library builders, built from native primitives so that
ob_run, zero crossings, strict C99 ob_codegen and ob_accelerate all work,
with Simulink's defaults, validateattributes-style 'ob_<name>:' errors,
and regression suites checked against recorded Simulink 26.2 traces:

 ** Nonlinear and logic: ob_backlash, ob_quantizer, ob_minmax,
    ob_saturation_dynamic, ob_dead_zone_dynamic, ob_sign,
    ob_coulomb_viscous_friction, ob_relational_operator and
    ob_logical_operator (n inputs from two-input chains, NXOR, vectors).
    Relational and Logical Operators output double 0/1.

 ** Routing and sources: ob_mux and ob_demux (any number of inputs, declared
    widths), ob_multiport_switch (control truncated toward zero, as
    Simulink records it), ob_pulse_generator and ob_chirp.

 ** Continuous and multirate: ob_second_order_integrator,
    ob_first_order_filter, and ob_rate_transition, which builds Simulink's
    Integrity/Deterministic Rate Transition modes between explicit rates.

New analysis functions ob_linearize (linmod), ob_findop (trim), ob_bode
(frequency response, margin/allmargin) and ob_stepinfo (stepinfo), checked
against Simulink 26.2 linmod/trim and Simulink traces.

The Simulink-style command API maps the new blocks by their Simulink R2026b
library paths and built-in/<BlockType> names (Backlash, Quantizer, MinMax,
Saturation Dynamic, Sign, Dead Zone Dynamic, Coulomb & Viscous Friction,
Relational and Logical Operator, Multiport Switch, Pulse Generator,
including sample-based pulses, Chirp Signal, Mux, Demux and
Integrator, Second-Order), and sim() accepts SaveFormat 'Dataset': yout and
the Scope logsout become Dataset-like structs with numElements,
getElement, get and getElementNames, recorded against Simulink 26.2. The
model default stays 'Array'. The handles survive Octave's binary/text
save and load; for MAT files, remove them and rebuild the Dataset with
ob_simulink ('dataset', s). A Mux or Demux signal whose shape differs
from the declared width stops sim with an error that names the block.

Not added: Zero-Order Hold (use a native Rate Transition), Moving Average,
Bus Creator/Selector (use ob_mux/ob_demux), sample-time reports and model
diagnostics.

See CHANGELOG.md for earlier preview release notes and doc/README.md
for the documentation index.
